    "caveats": [
      "All monetary fields are already stored in USD currency units, not cents. Customer and supplier account balances can be negative.",
      "`orders.o_totalprice` is an order-level stated total. Do not sum it after joining to `lineitem`, because each order total will repeat once per line item.",
      "Line-item gross value is `l_extendedprice`; net line revenue is `l_extendedprice * (1 - l_discount)`. Tax-inclusive revenue additionally multiplies by `(1 + l_tax)`. Choose the definition matching the question.",
      "`l_extendedprice` is the pre-discount extended amount for the line, whereas `p_retailprice` is a catalog per-unit retail price and should not be treated as realized sales revenue.",
      "To connect a line item to its actual supplier-part sourcing record, join `lineitem` to `partsupp` on both `l_partkey = ps_partkey` AND `l_suppkey = ps_suppkey`; joining on only part or only supplier creates incorrect matches and fan-out.",
      "`partsupp` is at part-supplier grain. Summing its inventory or supply cost after joining it to line items can duplicate inventory records; aggregate inventory at `partsupp` grain first when needed.",
      "A customer or supplier can be associated with a nation; customer geography and supplier geography are separate relationship paths. Use clear aliases when comparing their nations or regions.",
      "The data spans order dates from 1992-01-01 to 1998-08-02, shipment dates through 1998-11-29, and receipt dates through 1998-12-25. Date analyses should use the appropriate event date.",
      "Order keys range to 60,000 but there are 15,000 order rows, so order IDs are not consecutive and should never be used as a proxy for order count.",
      "`o_shippriority` is constant at 0 in the observed data and is not useful for segmentation."
    ],
    "example_questions": [
      "What were net line revenue and ordered quantity by customer market segment in each order year?",
